From: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb-moded: reject failed function and DHCP setup

Upstream-Status: Pending

The dynamic-mode path ignores failure from configfs function selection and
post-enumeration actions. Hoki NCM modes rely on configfs selection and start
`udhcp-daemon.service` during appsync post actions, so either failure can be
published as an activated mode.

This narrow candidate does not claim complete setter-error propagation. Hoki's
VID override is optional and is preloaded by `android-gadget-setup`; the dynamic
PID write also remains unchecked because both Hoki modes request the already
preloaded D001. These descriptor-write paths need separate impact review.

--- a/src/usb_moded-modesetting.c
+++ b/src/usb_moded-modesetting.c
@@ -764,7 +764,8 @@
 
     if( configfs_in_use() ) {
         /* Configfs based gadget configuration */
-        configfs_set_function(data->sysfs_value);
+        if( !configfs_set_function(data->sysfs_value) )
+            goto EXIT;
         configfs_set_productid(data->idProduct);
         char *id = config_get_android_vendor_id();
         configfs_set_vendorid(data->idVendorOverride ?: id);
@@ -848,7 +849,8 @@
         log_debug("Dynamic mode is appsync: do post actions");
         /* let's sleep for a bit (350ms) to allow interfaces to settle before running postsync */
         common_msleep(350);
-        appsync_activate_post(data->mode_name);
+        if( appsync_activate_post(data->mode_name) != 0 )
+            goto EXIT;
     }
 
     /* - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - *
